## Competitor Landscape
Competitor: Honeygain — Category: Centralized Bandwidth Sharing — Difference: Centralized entity, no token, fixed $/GB payout, KYC required — Market Segment: Residential Proxy / Bandwidth Monetization (MEDIUM) [Honeygain, https://honeygain.com/]; [Grass Blog, https://blog.grass.ai/how-grass-works/]
Competitor: PacketStream — Category: Centralized Bandwidth Sharing — Difference: Centralized, pay-per-request, no blockchain — Market Segment: Residential Proxy Network (MEDIUM) [PacketStream, https://packetstream.io/]; [Grass Blog, https://blog.grass.ai/how-grass-works/]
Competitor: Masa — Category: Decentralized AI Data Layer (DePIN) — Difference: Focus on user-owned data marketplace & fair AI, uses zkSQL — Market Segment: AI Training Data / Data Marketplace (MEDIUM) [Masa, https://masa.ai/]; [Messari, https://messari.io/project/masa/profile]
Competitor: Public AI — Category: Decentralized AI Data Labeling — Difference: Human-in-the-loop labeling, token incentives for annotation — Market Segment: AI Data Annotation (MEDIUM) [Public AI, https://public.ai/]; [Messari, https://messari.io/project/public-ai/profile]
Competitor: Synesis One — Category: Decentralized Data Crowdsourcing — Difference: Gamified data annotation (Kanon NFT), Solana-based — Market Segment: AI Data Crowdsourcing (MEDIUM) [Synesis One, https://synesis.one/]; [Messari, https://messari.io/project/synesis-one/profile]
Competitor: Theta EdgeCloud — Category: DePIN Compute/Bandwidth — Difference: Focus on video streaming & AI compute, not web scraping — Market Segment: Decentralized Compute / CDN (MEDIUM) [Theta, https://www.thetatoken.org/edgecloud]; [Messari, https://messari.io/project/theta/profile]
Competitor: Akash Network — Category: DePIN Compute — Difference: Decentralized cloud compute marketplace, not bandwidth scraping — Market Segment: Decentralized Cloud Compute (MEDIUM) [Akash, https://akash.network/]; [Messari, https://messari.io/project/akash/profile]

